{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/682753-can-anyone-recommend-anymore-inspirational-for-demon-the-decent","id":682753,"title":"Can anyone recommend anymore inspirational for demon the decent ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-30T01:02:59-07:00","id":682753,"title":"Can anyone recommend anymore inspirational for demon the decent ?","content":"I've been watching the anime Parasyte and I think the body horror and the some of the themes in this anime fits demon very well but I wanted to find some more inspirational material for demon can anyone recommend anything ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T01:57:59-07:00","id":682833,"title":"","content":"The Bone Clocks by David Mitchell. It reads like a perfect representation of being a mortal in the World of Darkness. Weird, spooky things happen on the periphery of your life but you can mostly pretend everything is normal so long as you don't think too hard about them. There is a shadow war between two supernatural factions playing out in the background of the main character's life, a war with a lot of spy tactics. One group of immortals take on new faces and identities and both sides are constantly prepared for both mundane and magical attacks. Plus there's something in the book that sounds exactly like infrastructure (complete with its own Guardian Angel) and I think it even gets described at one point as an &quot;occult machine&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T04:27:25-07:00","id":682907,"title":"","content":"I know it gets name checked in the source book but since that time Person of Interest has gotten even more like Live Action Demon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T05:00:43-07:00","id":682996,"title":"","content":"I love person of interest. I can't wait to see a few of the actors at comic con this year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T09:56:58-07:00","id":683257,"title":"","content":"The BBC series <b>Utopia</b> has a plot that goes off the rails fast into some silly stuff, but the aesthetics of the show are fantastic at conveying an oppressive and paranoid atmosphere with an occasional sense of wonder and mystery, and the actions of the conspiracy's enforcers drive home how the agents of the God-Machine don't always have to be plugged into mortal power structures to get shit done, as long as they're willing to just act like they belong. The soundtrack is really good.<br /> <br /> <b>Burn Notice</b> is a fun thriller series with a lot of asides from the perspective of a professional spy, very useful for giving you ideas as to cool things a demon might be out doing.<br /> <br /> If you don't mind opaque plots that require you to read between the lines and lack definite answers, the video game <b>killer7</b> has awkward gameplay but oozes style. You play as a government wetworks operative with multiple distinct identities, each with their own appearance, personality and weird abilities. Curve bullets like in Wanted? More like curve <i>rocket-propelled grenades</i>. At heaven's request we will purge the unwanted. We must get rid of bad trees by their roots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T11:28:14-07:00","id":683344,"title":"","content":"Transistor would be interesting to look at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T16:23:09-07:00","id":685030,"title":"","content":"<b>Black Mirror</b> just screams GMC.<br /> <br /> Try <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>ZER0ES</b></span> by Chuck Wendig.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Dennou Coil (anime) stupidly hard to find, but essential viewing if you ever want to run an Heirs to Hell campaign<br /> <br /> City of Stairs by Robert Jackson Bennett<br /> <br /> Book of Spies Edited by Alan Furst (short stories, so easy enough to mine for individual adventures)<br /> <br /> For nonfiction try:<br /> <br /> The 9/11 Wars by Jason Burke for a very complete look at how the 9/11 attacks and aftermath changed the espionage landscape.<br /> <br /> Near and Distant Neighbors by Jonathan Haslam (Soviet Intelligence. Really, really good)<br /> <br /> Data and Goliath by Bruce Schneier (any of his works are excellent for Techgnostic Espionage)<br /> <br /> Future Crimes by Marc Goodman (Excellent look at how the Deva Corp might go about hunting for Demons, and what the Unchained might have to do to stay off the radar)<br /> <br /> Board games:<br /> <br /> Tragedy Looper - a board game where a team of 1-3 players compete against the Mastermind (a fourth player). Since the 1-3 have no idea what's going on, and have to deduce what's going on based on how the mastermind reacts to their blind movements, it can really have a very strong GMC feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 01-16-2016, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T23:35:26-07:00","id":686605,"title":"","content":"The spy comedy Chuck ended up giving me a lot of thoughts for Cover and for plots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T10:27:51-07:00","id":691393,"title":"","content":"Video games: Portal, Portal 2, Talos Principle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T00:31:33-07:00","id":693527,"title":"","content":"I don't see how Portal/Portal 2 helps? Maybe the alien intelligence of Glados? But, I don't really see <i>it. </i><br /> But what of Talos Principle? Is it good?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T00:55:59-07:00","id":693535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/682753-can-anyone-recommend-anymore-inspirational-for-demon-the-decent?p=693527#post693527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how Portal/Portal 2 helps? Maybe the alien intelligence of Glados? But, I don't really see <i>it. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>Aperture Science is not a well-run company and the army of mantis-men is one of many horrifying testaments to the efficiencies necessitated by this fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T01:56:01-07:00","id":693563,"title":"","content":"The book Ancillary Justice is pretty good inspiration for understanding what it must be like to go from being an Angel to a Demon. The main character is a rogue AI in a human body navigating a rather religious science fiction society with the intent to destroy something much greater than themselves. Before they went rogue they were connected to the system and possessed thousands of bodies. Suddenly constrained to one leaves them feeling exceptionally vulnerable, particularly in respect to the loss of information they suffered when they went from having a thousand eyes and ears to a single perspective. There are some amusing habits of the main character (particularly their inability to grasp gender and its role in any of the many languages they speak) that would make for great Glitches in a Demon character. Plus there's a fairly strong espionage bent to the main plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T04:35:33-07:00","id":694728,"title":"","content":"Thinking about the mortal tradecraft parts of it, I got fixated on The Blue Ant trilogy from William Gibson. Especially Spook Country.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T02:13:52-07:00","id":695861,"title":"","content":"And what about music? I think that such artists like &quot;The electric hellfire club&quot;, &quot;Ministry&quot; and &quot;VNV Nation&quot; will suite the setting just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8398-bitter001","name":"bitter001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8398_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T20:47:02-08:00","id":794582,"title":"","content":"Gravity falls - two Latents spend the summer visiting their Great Uncle, a Messenger Tempter who lives in a town full of malfunctioning Infrastructure, cultists, and cryptids. Recommended for running an Heirs/Innocents/GMC chronicle. Great for a scene of Soup Up being used on a golf cart.<br /> <br /> The Black Watchman - An augmented reality game in the vein of the canceled Majestic - 12. It's also a Spinoff of the Secret World MMORPG, which is another good, if flawed, inspiration.<br /> <br /> Deutchland 83 - a German television show about espionage in the days before the reunification of Germany. Nuclear war tension, secrets, all good stuff.<br /> <br /> Subnormality - a Webcomic. Visually inspirational of a world where the mythic and mundane rub shoulders, often without the latter realizing it. The current strip: Museum of the Theoretical would make a perfect piece of infrastructure.<br /> <br /> Heaven and Earth and Potters Lake. Heaven and Earth was an old RPG that tried to do Biblical Horror. Besides the utility of mining ideas from an RPG that delves into maltheist horror, the town of Potters Lake is pure standout of a setting. It's a small mid-western town instead of a major city, but it's <i>every bit</i> as good as Seattle for Demon. It's as a weird place where the inhabitants have no choice but to take it in stride. The town grocery store alone is worth the price of admission.<br /> <br /> Welcome to Nightvale. A podcast. Did we not mention this already?<br /> <br /> Mystery Show. Another podcast about a woman investigating very mundane mysteries, such as how did a video rental store disappear overnight. What sells it how she gets out to investigate, research, and interview. Her rule for the show is that she doesn't use the internet to solves the mystery. Make the object of each investigation an infrastructure of some kind, add a few dead bodies, a cult or two, an albino alligator in the sewers and a sinister hunter angel and any one of her mysteries will make a damn fine DtD story or two.<br /> <br /> Pandemic Legacy. This what I imagine running a tier 3 Free Agency must feel like: global reach, global resources and you're constantly overwhelmed. From the outside everyone thinks your organization is invincible, but you know that's just on paper. Your most capable agents have their own agendas and are the most likely to just... disappear.<br /> <br /> 14 by Peter Clines","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 01-11-2016, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T21:29:06-08:00","id":794595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/682753-can-anyone-recommend-anymore-inspirational-for-demon-the-decent?p=683344#post683344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Transistor would be interesting to look at.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Once there was a great engineer. Arithmetic was his medium and a city was his canvas.<br /> <br /> [\u2026] The nature of his work led him to notice certain patterns. The will of the people changed in cycles.<br /> <br /> [\u2026] He studied this formula closely for it filled him with a deep sense of wonder and an even deeper sense of dread.<br /> <br /> [\u2026] He saw beyond the confines of the city into something more, and there before him was something extraordinary.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T04:52:44-08:00","id":794763,"title":"","content":"Mr Robot just screams Demon to me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T07:35:24-08:00","id":794819,"title":"","content":"The Adjustment Bureau, a 2011 movie. And the short story that inspired it, &quot;Adjustment Team&quot;, by Philip K. Dick. It can give you plenty of ideas for Agencies, Boltholes, and Infrastructure. Maybe even ideas for Angels/Demons and Stigmatics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T08:20:41-08:00","id":794834,"title":"","content":"Vertigo's run of Doom Patrol has a pretty diverse group of characters psychologically and physically. Could be a great source for demonic forms and how embeds/exploits could look like. The story could also serve as material on how to deal with Glitches that really change an Unchained's appearance. That being said pretty much any Vertigo series could be used as source material. Mike Allred's current project Art Ops is really wonderful and out there in its depiction of a secret cell of art operatives. <br /> <br /> The movie Sicario gives a solid look at spy and military violence with a wonderful narrative to boot. Benicio del Toro's character could be great inspiration for how efficiently a Destroyer would move and how complicated a violent character can be. If you look at it from Emily Blunt's character, the story could be of how a Shield/Sword angel descends after walking away from the violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T08:59:12-08:00","id":794867,"title":"","content":"&quot;Welcome to Night Vale&quot; makes for good ideas for weird goings-on and Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> &quot;Dogs are not allowed in the Dog Park. People are not allowed in the Dog Park. It is possible you may see Hooded Figures in the Dog Park. Do not approach them. Do not approach the Dog Park.&quot;<br /> <br /> Tall, winged beings that are DEFINITELY NOT angels...<br /> <br /> A house that doesn't exist. I mean, it seems like it exists, like, it's right there when you look at it, and it would make more sense for it to exist than not, but it definitely doesn't exist. <br /> <br /> A man in a tan jacket carrying a deerskin suitcase full of flies.<br /> <br /> &quot;Come on down to the hole in the vacant lot out back of the Ralph's and huddle with Us.&quot;<br /> <br /> A radio station on which a monotone female voice reads off seemingly random numbers occasionally interspersed with chimes.<br /> <br /> A man who can see the glowing arrows, dotted lines, and circles in the sky. The great chart that explains it all...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2573-inkpenavenger","name":"inkpenavenger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2573_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T00:16:02-08:00","id":795434,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0830361/\" target=\"_blank\">The Lost Room</a> is an enjoyable little mini-series that is full of weird science and happenings under the veneer of a very, very normal standard location. It's just a hotel room, after all.<br /> <br /> Keep the pencil, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T11:10:36-08:00","id":801515,"title":"","content":"Reservoir Dogs is really good, for some super violent intra-group conflict where no one really trusts each other. <br /> <br /> And Archer, if a more lighthearted zany kind of thing works for your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T13:51:21-08:00","id":801582,"title":"","content":"The new James Bond comic is a great source for spy visuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T14:30:19-08:00","id":801601,"title":"","content":"One scene from Mission Impossible: Rogue Nation established the series as Demon inspiration for me. The powerhouse female operative acting opposite of Tom Cruise offers him a third option between allowing the bad guy (an Angel or Exile) to win to save his friends, and trying to stop him and sacrificing himself.<br /> <br /> Paraphrasing loosely: &quot;You could run away with me. We can be anyone, we can do anything. All you have to do is say yes, right now, and we can be free.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T14:36:28-08:00","id":801604,"title":"","content":"The show American Gothic could be an example of a hell made by a Tempter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T15:16:56-08:00","id":804740,"title":"","content":"I just finished the latest episode of Elementary (Season 4 Episode 7). That girl is a tempter Demon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1092-tribute-of-a-dark-heart","name":"Tribute of a Dark Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T21:12:52-08:00","id":804993,"title":"","content":"Oh, I really like that idea. It would probably be even more infuriating if she was, if only because she could actually be who she says she is via a Soul Pact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T08:22:42-08:00","id":805260,"title":"","content":"The Americans - S1/2 available on Amazon Prime. Deep cover cold war era spies, posing as a married couple, with children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T15:12:19-08:00","id":805524,"title":"","content":"Angelmaker by Nick Harkaway. Even aside from the incredibly evocative name, it's filled with examples of clockwork and other &quot;simple&quot; technology taken to ludicrously advanced extremes, strange shadowy figures, automaton monks, mysterious organisations, and arcane conspiracies. There's even a bit of spy action, but it's really more James Bond action than it is real espionage. The first half of the book is where it really excels as inspiration though. Before the secrets behind each figure are revealed, it really does feel like the main character has been caught in a vortex of competing supernatural forces with hidden agendas and incomprehensible powers.<br /> <br /> And the bees are totally Infrastructure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T03:49:58-08:00","id":805960,"title":"","content":"The Americans: Set during the cold war, this entire show is about maintaining the deepest level of cover. Even their children don't know their real identity. I can't think of anything more perfect for Demon than this show.<br /> <br /> Wayward Pines: I'm sorry to say that I didn't like this show, however I kept watching it because it was very inspirational for the GMC for me. I really can't say anything more without dropping spoilers but the themes and tone of this show kept giving me ideas for GMC.<br /> <br /> Mr Robot: Paranoia, hacking, secret organizations and never being quite sure what's real in this show made it another good watch for Demon in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T15:31:09-08:00","id":810844,"title":"","content":"The Big Short.<br /> <br /> Ok, yes, a little weird. But it really is a wonderful example of the impenetrability and complexity of interlinked human institutions with unfathomable impacts on the life of people who know nothing about them. The Financial Sector as Concealment Infrastructure, obfuscating what is actually going on and protected by people too greedy or too stupid to actually investigate in their own right. Then the housing market as Logistical Infrastructure, producing the GFC as Output.<br /> <br /> Mostly, this is just a vibe rather than something I'd actually use in a game. But there is one scene involving an almost entirely deserted housing development that just <i>screams</i> Infrastructure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}